it's been well over a month since the  release of the galaxy s 20 ultra and  while this phone itself is actually a  killer phone the launch of it was I'd  say quite unfortunate it was clear from  the very beginning that Samsung was  taking a pretty big risk on the ultra I  mean they priced it at a starting price  of $1400 and that's quite expensive even  compared to the best iPhones out there  which have themselves been criticized  for being too expensive  since the thousand-dollar iPhone 10 so  Samsung knowing how big of a risk this  was put all of their chips in the  marketing campaign of the s20 ultras new  features like the cameras and 5g making  it seem like this was the best  smartphone on the market now if your  smartphone is so good that it can prove  itself as the best smartphone in the  world  then the $1400 price tag might be  justified and people will buy it this  was the trick that Apple pulled with the  iPhone 10 at release it was the most  expensive smartphone ever but because it  was so good it actually was the  best-selling smartphone of the year but  in the case of the Galaxy S tony ultra a  couple of very unfortunate things  happened that nobody was expecting but  before I get into that I want to talk  about the s20 ultra itself and what I  really enjoyed about this phone since we  got our hands on it first off I love the  design it's just so fine-tuned compared  to before I personally love large camera  bumps and I feel like the one on the s20  ultra just seems so substantial and  premium I also like the button layout  with all the buttons being on one side  and the power button being in the  perfect spot for my thumb and I  absolutely love the massive 6.9 inch  display Samsung really nailed it this  year with the subtle and clean looking  hole punch camera in the center instead  of on the side this looks so much  cleaner than the iPhones knotch  that's getting quite a bit old already  and Samsung managed to pull off really  thin bezels while also not curving the  display as much as before this is great  because I no longer touch the edges of  the display like I did with the s10 plus  and the display itself is just amazing  it's super bright in its very color  accurate as  well the sheer size of it actually makes  it a decent device to watch Netflix on  and then couple that with incredibly  loud speakers and you've got the best  phone for watching videos and I'm still  extremely impressed with how Samsung  managed to make the earphone speakers so  loud while being so thin that it's  almost invisible I honestly think that  the ask Tony altra is the best phone for  gaming that's ever been made because of  the combination of the massive display  the excellent speakers the subtle  hole-punch camera and the new 120 Hertz  display I played three different games  on both the iPhone 11 Pro Max and the  s20 ultra for an hour each to test the  battery life of each of these phones  even though the Ultra was running these  games at 120 Hertz while the iPhone was  running them at 60 the ultra drained  just a little bit more battery life  which was extremely impressive and it  did it while running the game smoothly  and the phone itself didn't heat up as  much as the iPhone so for all those  reasons it's the best phone for gaming  yet now in terms of performance both the  iPhone and the s2000 are now so fast  that it really doesn't improve the  everyday experience of using the phone  any more than last year's models but  what does improve it is the 120 Hertz  display this feature by itself makes the  ultra feel so much more snappy compared  to the iPhone when swiping through your  home screen or scrolling through apps  like Facebook and it's also nice to know  that you've got top-of-the-line specs  like 12 or 16 gigs of ram Wi-Fi 6 IP 68  water resistance and 5g connectivity for  those who agree with that and now the  only thing I haven't mentioned is the  biggest thing that Samsung marketed the  world's best camera system and with this  camera system Samsung took a major risk  but before I get into what happened with  the cameras I want to get into the first  unfortunate thing that happened when  Samson launched the s20 ultra they  couldn't have made the risk of launching  a $1400 phone at a worse time  the corona virus pandemic turned out  quite a bit worse than we all expected  with the economy taking a massive hit  the national multi-family housing  council recently released  showing that nearly one-third of us  apartment renters didn't pay the rent at  all in April showing just how bad the  economy has gotten in such a short  amount of time so the truth of the  matter is if the economy is suffering  this badly who is gonna be buying a  brand new cell phone let alone one that  costs $1,400 a couple of weeks ago  Samsung held a private conference call  where they reportedly saw very  disappointing sales of the galaxy s 20  series phones and while they haven't  released official sales numbers yet it's  estimated that they only sold 60% of the  sales of the s10 Series last year now I  know that it's not just Samsung phones  taking a hit the entire smartphone  industry got hit as well including Apple  with researchers expecting global  consumers to purchase 33 million fewer  phones this year so with all that out of  the way let's get into the second  unfortunate thing that happens at the  launch of the s20 altra they focused way  too much marketing on the camera making  it seem like the s Tony all sure had by  far the best camera on any smartphone so  with that came massive expectations from  consumers and initial reviewers however  they also chose to put in a brand new  camera system that they've never used  before and because of that this software  wasn't ready for the release so when  reviewers got their hands on the S 20  ultra almost every initial review  mentioned camera issues especially with  auto focusing this is really bad news  for Samsung since quite a lot of people  decided to wait until the issues were  resolved before investing $1,400 into  this phone we tried it ourselves and ran  a blind test comparing the s20 ultra the  s 20 plus and the note 10 plus which  quickly became very popular gating  almost half a million views and  surprisingly the note actually won the  test at that point  Samsung promised a huge software update  that would fix the camera for good and  now over a month later that software  update finally came so just recently we  did another camera test before and after  the  update to see what's changed and while  it did improve the autofocus performance  is nowhere near where it should be and  much worse compared to the iPhone 11 pro  max so the camera performance is still  disappointing after that update so maybe  they have more camera updates planned I  don't know but now that it's been five  and a half weeks since we received the  phone it's honestly too late the s20  ultras reputation has already been  damaged so much especially in this  economy that I don't think the sales of  this phone will ever recover but let's  pretend for a minute that the camera was  so good that it blew every phone away in  that case this would probably be the  phone of the year but with the camera  that is nowhere near as good as Samson  said it would be even people who have  the extra cash to buy the s20 ultra  should just buy something else like the  s20 plus now that phone is actually  great so if you want to see our review  of the s20 plus tap the like' button and  click the circle above to subscribe so  you don't miss out on that review and  make sure to check out our s20 ultra  camera comparisons right over there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]
 

